Niobium — local DeepSeek Harness distributions
==========================================

This distribution includes and statically links the following components:

- iSH / iSH-ARM64 — GPLv3 with the additional iOS terms in
  `ios/ThirdParty/dsh-ios/ish-arm64/LICENSE.IOS`.
- DSH iOS host code — Copyright the DSH contributors, GPLv3, from
  https://github.com/everettjf/dsh-ios.
- Alpine Linux userland and packages — various free software licenses, shipped
  inside the generated guest image `root.tar.gz`.
- DeepSeek Harness (`@deepseek-ai/dsh`) and npm dependencies — MIT and other
  licenses, shipped inside the generated guest image.
- hterm and libapps — BSD-3-Clause.
- libarchive — BSD-2-Clause.

Because the app links iSH, the combined iOS application is distributed under the
GNU General Public License version 3. The source for the complete corresponding
application is this repository, including the `ios/ThirdParty/dsh-ios`
submodule. The guest image is reproducibly built by
`ios/scripts/build-local-dsh.sh`; the exact DSH submodule revision is recorded
by git.

The Android native UI and runtime supervisor are MIT-licensed and do not link
iSH. The Android APK also distributes separate PRoot executables (GPL-2.0),
libtalloc (LGPL/GPL components), libandroid-shmem (BSD-3-Clause), and the same
Alpine/DSH guest image. These components retain their respective licenses;
the APK as a collection must not be described as entirely MIT-licensed.

Exact Android package versions, checksums, source archive checksums and the
Termux packaging revision are in config/android-runtime.json. Run
python3 tools/prepare-android-runtime.py --sources to obtain the corresponding
upstream source archives. Android release assets include those sources,
Termux build recipes/patches, and this repository's supervisor source.
The PRoot fork is https://github.com/termux/proot; Termux packaging is
https://github.com/termux/termux-packages. Neither requires the Termux app.
